From 09ec201c3554aa5262018a4f4f58695fed27af9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 18:36:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] feat: move static UI copy from next-intl JSON to Supabase
 + Lara
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per explicit request: the static text across landing/configurator/
proposal (already wired to useTranslations() in earlier commits) was
being served from committed en.json/it.json message files. Now it's
Supabase-backed, same pattern as experience_content_translations:

- New tables site_copy (key, en_text) / site_copy_translations
  (key, locale, text, translation_status) — SQL to run once in
  Supabase is in supabase-migrations/2026_site_copy.sql.
- src/lib/translations/siteCopy.ts: getSiteCopyMessages(locale) reads
  both tables and reconstructs the same nested message shape next-intl
  already expects (landing/configurator/proposal/common namespaces),
  so every existing useTranslations("...")/t("key") call site in the
  components is unchanged — only the data source moved.
- src/scripts/seed-site-copy.mjs: one-time migration script. Flattens
  the current en.json, upserts it into site_copy, and calls Lara
  directly to populate site_copy_translations for "it". Idempotent —
  safe to re-run, only retranslates keys whose English text changed.
- /api/translate-site-copy: manual re-sync endpoint for a single key
  (or "*" for all) after editing en_text directly in the Supabase
  table — there's no admin UI for this by design.
- Root layout no longer imports en.json for /admin; passes {} since
  admin never calls useTranslations() anyway.
- Retired the old prebuild step (translate-messages.mjs, which
  generated it.json at build time) and it.json itself — both
  superseded by the DB-backed pipeline above. en.json stays only as
  the one-time seed source for seed-site-copy.mjs.

Requires manual action: run supabase-migrations/2026_site_copy.sql in
the Supabase SQL editor, then `npm run seed:site-copy` once with
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY / LARA_ACCESS_KEY_ID
/ LARA_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET set, before this will show any translated (or
even English) text — site_copy starts out empty.
